cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Explainable ECG denoising via a supervised multi-encoder
  autoencoder with encoding masking
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lim
    given-names: Minsik
    affiliation: Gachon University
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # email: your.institutional@address
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Limminsik/MEAE_XAI"
abstract: >-
  A supervised multi-encoder autoencoder (MEAE) that separates a
  noisy single-lead ECG into interpretable components. Each of the
  four parallel encoders is assigned one reference source before
  training (clean ECG, baseline wander, muscle artefact, electrode
  motion), so the assignment diagonal of the component-to-reference
  table is itself the evidence of separation. Denoising is then a
  pure inference-time operation: zeroing the three noise encodings
  and decoding, with no retraining and no change to any weight. The
  denoised signal is evaluated on three axes - component alignment,
  reconstruction fidelity against the clean reference, and
  reference-free signal quality indices together with clinical
  morphology measurements.
keywords:
  - electrocardiography
  - ECG denoising
  - blind source separation
  - multi-encoder autoencoder
  - explainable AI
  - signal quality index
